<http://www.spektrix.com/factorytheatre/event/146002ABJNJKRSBJJHKTLSKHPNPLHMPPK> a
    schema:Event;
  schema:name "Documents Perform 3";
  schema:description """
	<span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">The Setting: A blank stage with a giant screen. Projected onto the screen are two documents containing excerpts of the Massey Commission in English and French. An online ensemble of “hacktors” made up of artists, artistic producers, cultural leaders, and policymakers begin “hacking” and rewriting the Commission in unison, in real time before a live audience. </span></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Documents Perform 3</span></span> asks a simple question: Who gets to define the value of culture, and how? The 1951 Royal Commission on National Development in the Arts, Letters and Sciences (better known as the Massey Commission) established a foundation for how Canada has understood arts, culture, and national identity for more than seventy years. What happens when those historically excluded from its vision become its editors and, in turn, the co-authors of a new cultural blueprint?<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>As edits unfold on screen, spectators will witness not simply the deconstruction of a historical document, but a public negotiation over the values that ought to guide Canada's cultural future. At the conclusion of the performance, the newly authored text will be read aloud and publicly ratified as the first iteration of an evolving cultural charter, one that will continue to be collectively rewritten, contested, and expanded over the seven-year life of The Arts Impact Partnership (TAIP) as new voices, communities, and understandings of cultural value emerge.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Performance Action | Projections in both Français and English<span><br/></span>Sensory Warning: Fog/haze<span><br/></span>Duration: 120 mins (approx.)<span><br/></span>Age Recommendation: 10+<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-09-27T14:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/factorytheatre/files/77cbe6b3-bf23-4fc0-bf03-67ef7245e860.jpg>;
